                <pb facs="0175" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr., to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-05">5 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>433. Following statement issued by PPC for your information.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“To General Marshall, Excellency: During the past few months your excellency
                        has with deep understanding exerted yourself to the utmost assisting our
                        Supreme Commander to overcome the various kinds of military difficulties
                        which have arisen following the War. By doing so, you not only have
                        exchanged the friendly relations between China and the United States but
                        also have made a true contribution toward the achievement of unity in China.
                        We the members of the People’s Political Council now in session, having come
                        from all parts of China, share a common feeling of gratitude to your
                        excellency for your enthusiasm and determination as well as your spirit of
                        unselfish service. In accordance with a resolution passed by the People’s
                        Political Council in plenary session, we hereby address this airgram to you
                        to convey our appreciation. From the People’s Political Council of the
                        Republic of China, April 2, 1946. Sealed People’s Political Council.”</p>
                </quote>
            </div>
